WEBVTT

00:00:09.917 --> 00:00:14.292
We put forth all of our efforts.

00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:17.083
We're satisfied with our victory
in the school festival.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.042
Oh?

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:18.750
"School Festival: Overall Results"

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.042
"School Festival: Overall Results"
It seems to have been a very close one.

00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:24.625
Only because the E Class had a battle plan.

00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:27.208
Winning by a huge margin
would have been nearly im--

00:00:27.208 --> 00:00:29.083
Incorrect.

00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:31.083
They were running a restaurant.

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.958
It's easy enough to spread nasty rumors,

00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:36.792
and a case of food poisoning
would have ruined them.

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:40.292
You neglected the more... harmful endeavors.

00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:41.625
Is he for real?

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:45.500
Harmful? Were we supposed to
poison the E Class's food?!

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.083
Sir, your education is inconsistent.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.750
I don't know how,

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.792
but the E Class has grown stronger
by leaps and bounds in just one year,

00:00:56.792 --> 00:01:00.000
enough to compete with us,
the chosen A Class.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.208
As irritating as it is, I feel
my abilities have grown as well.

00:01:04.208 --> 00:01:07.625
I cannot deny that they
have become my motivation.

00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:09.375
These mighty foes, my min--

00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:13.375
I mean, <i>friends</i>: such connections
have made me stronger.

00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:15.917
You were totally going to say "minions"!

00:01:15.917 --> 00:01:19.708
You do not become strong
by winning over the weak.

00:01:19.708 --> 00:01:25.875
That's my conclusion... and where
I diverge from the path you teach.

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:31.917
Asano, would you leave us
for about three minutes?

00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.083
I'd like to speak with your four friends here.

00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:37.875
You know. Just a little chat.

00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:42.792
Go on, Asano. What's three minutes?

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:52.083
What's going on?

00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:55.250
You may enter, Asano.

00:01:58.542 --> 00:02:00.875
Ren! Seo!

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:05.667
Kill the E Class, kill the E Class,
kill the E Class...

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.667
What--What did you...

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:11.042
I just fanned the flames
of their hatred, that's all.

00:02:11.042 --> 00:02:13.125
It only takes a whispered word or three

00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:17.125
for those "connections" of yours to collapse.

00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:21.333
The strength I teach is nothing so fragile.

00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:24.958
I'll handle the end-of-term exams.

00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:29.292
Without strength,
you lack both meaning and merit.

00:02:29.292 --> 00:02:31.917
I'll teach you exactly that--from square one.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.167
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:52.000
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.417
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:02:57.417 --> 00:03:00.083
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:02.792
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:03:02.792 --> 00:03:06.583
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:10.583
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:13.542
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:03:13.542 --> 00:03:18.792
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:03:18.792 --> 00:03:24.375
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:03:24.375 --> 00:03:29.792
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:35.292
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:03:35.292 --> 00:03:37.917
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.583
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:43.375
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:03:43.375 --> 00:03:45.958
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.667
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.375
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:54.208
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:03:54.208 --> 00:03:59.208
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.000
"11th Period: End-of-Term Time/2nd Period"
"by Kotaro Takebayashi"

00:04:08.375 --> 00:04:10.875
For as long as I can remember,

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:13.708
my house has been a classroom.

00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:17.000
My father the teacher... and I his student.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.417
And when he had nothing
in particular to teach me,

00:04:20.417 --> 00:04:22.917
we didn't talk at all.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:32.042
Oh, stop here, please.

00:04:32.042 --> 00:04:33.458
Yes, sir.

00:04:34.292 --> 00:04:36.000
Hey.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.833
Good to see you're as well as ever.

00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:42.750
This town, though--
Change is in the air. I can feel it.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:46.625
Times like this, I stand to
make a good sum of money...

00:04:46.625 --> 00:04:49.333
...so here's some pocket change for you, too.

00:04:50.542 --> 00:04:54.125
For your favorite game of chance.

00:04:54.125 --> 00:04:57.250
That's the only way you can
feel the joy of being alive--

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:01.500
though I <i>am </i>the one who taught you that.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.042
Just a moment, here--

00:05:03.042 --> 00:05:05.250
Could you repeat that?

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.125
I need another billion.

00:05:08.125 --> 00:05:10.833
This assassination is
really warming up now, no?

00:05:10.833 --> 00:05:13.958
Who knows what could happen.

00:05:13.958 --> 00:05:17.333
I must consider the risks to my students...

00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:20.000
...and it costs money to keep secrets.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.583
I've lived here a long time, so I can tell:

00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:27.500
You're moving ahead
with some kind of major plans.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.417
But that doesn't mean--

00:05:28.417 --> 00:05:29.792
Enough, Sonokawa.

00:05:29.792 --> 00:05:33.583
How many times are we going to be
shaken down for more hush money?

00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:37.375
By the time March rolls around,
we'll have paid him more than the bounty!

00:05:37.375 --> 00:05:42.917
Remember, he's graciously
allowing us to use this school.

00:05:43.917 --> 00:05:48.667
Wire it to my account, if you please.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.208
What shrewd instincts.

00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:55.333
Even picked up on the final
assassination project in progress here.

00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:56.958
He's quite a man,

00:05:56.958 --> 00:06:00.375
having the entire Ministry of Defense
in the palm of his hand.

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:05.208
All right, now for
an overview of the past year.

00:06:05.208 --> 00:06:08.000
Next up is the classwork battle.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.125
Are you prepared to take the top spot, Karma?

00:06:10.125 --> 00:06:11.417
"Tentacle"
Are you prepared to take the top spot, Karma?

00:06:11.417 --> 00:06:16.167
"Tentacle"
Gee, I dunno. Idiots like me don't understand hard stuff.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.875
For your first-term midterms,

00:06:18.875 --> 00:06:23.000
I gave everyone the goal
of making the top fifty.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.542
I apologize for that.
I was too impatient for results,

00:06:27.542 --> 00:06:30.125
and I didn't count on
your opponents being so strong.

00:06:30.125 --> 00:06:35.208
But things are different now.
You've matured in brain and spirit.

00:06:35.208 --> 00:06:37.208
You should be able to meet your goals

00:06:37.208 --> 00:06:39.833
in the face of any plot or setback.

00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:42.417
With heads held high,
you will all come in the top fifty,

00:06:42.417 --> 00:06:46.000
you will receive your tickets
back to the main campus,

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.292
and you will graduate as the E Class.

00:06:49.292 --> 00:06:51.333
If only it were that easy.

00:06:51.333 --> 00:06:52.208
Huh?

00:06:52.208 --> 00:06:55.542
The A Class has a new teacher--

00:06:55.542 --> 00:06:58.208
and you won't believe who it is.

00:06:58.208 --> 00:07:01.458
As of today, I'll be taking over your lessons.

00:07:01.458 --> 00:07:04.542
Good luck, A Class.

00:07:04.542 --> 00:07:07.167
So that's what it's come to.

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:10.958
Honestly, I want no part
of his brainwashing education.

00:07:10.958 --> 00:07:14.875
His weird charisma,
controlling people with a word or a glance...

00:07:14.875 --> 00:07:18.583
His teaching skills put him on a par
with our Mach-20 Koro Sensei.

00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:19.542
Nrrrgh!

00:07:19.542 --> 00:07:22.042
If <i>he's </i>their teacher...

00:07:22.042 --> 00:07:25.458
...they've probably already
lost the will to defy him.

00:07:27.917 --> 00:07:30.792
It's ten times easier than our usual lessons...

00:07:30.792 --> 00:07:33.833
...but twenty times faster!

00:07:33.833 --> 00:07:39.875
Hashizume, Tanaka, Fujii, Kondo, Okuno--
you seem a little behind.

00:07:39.875 --> 00:07:40.583
Huh?

00:07:40.583 --> 00:07:42.792
How can he tell with his back to us?!

00:07:42.792 --> 00:07:45.375
I-It's just too fast!

00:07:45.375 --> 00:07:49.542
Maybe if we were at the Big Five's level,
but this is impossible for us!

00:07:49.542 --> 00:07:51.458
You think it's impossible

00:07:51.458 --> 00:07:54.875
because you don't understand
what it means to fight.

00:07:54.875 --> 00:07:58.208
Why don't we talk in
the hallway for three minutes?

00:07:58.208 --> 00:08:00.583
Let's have a little chat.

00:08:05.333 --> 00:08:09.375
Kill the E Class,
kill the E Class, kill the E Class...

00:08:09.375 --> 00:08:12.458
Kill the E Class,
kill the E Class, kill the E Class...

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:16.042
You study not just for your own sake.

00:08:16.042 --> 00:08:19.750
You will grow even more powerful
than the E Class has become

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.958
and demolish them.

00:08:21.958 --> 00:08:26.375
When the lower grades see you,
the A Class, doing just that,

00:08:26.375 --> 00:08:29.333
they'll know you were right

00:08:29.333 --> 00:08:32.333
and devote themselves to joining your ranks.

00:08:32.333 --> 00:08:36.083
Your actions will boost the level of humanity.

00:08:36.083 --> 00:08:41.000
Oh, and Asano? You can go home
and study on your own.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.625
With your skills, you'll keep the top spot
if you just stay on your guard.

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:50.000
I'll be the one to lead everyone upward.

00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:55.333
You know, they're kind of similar,

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:57.333
the principal and Koro Sensei.

00:08:57.333 --> 00:08:58.458
How so?

00:08:58.458 --> 00:09:03.875
They both have extraordinary powers,
but are regular teachers.

00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:06.667
With the principal's quick wits,

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:09.792
he could have been prime minister
or a business bigshot.

00:09:09.792 --> 00:09:13.667
But he's devoted himself
to education at just one academy.

00:09:13.667 --> 00:09:17.625
No wonder he's so unrelenting.

00:09:17.625 --> 00:09:20.208
Huh? It's Asano.

00:09:20.208 --> 00:09:21.750
What do <i>you </i>want?

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:25.042
You're not the kind of guy
who'd run recon on us.

00:09:27.208 --> 00:09:32.208
It pains me to say this... but I have a request.

00:09:33.458 --> 00:09:37.417
I'll cut to the chase. That monster...

00:09:37.417 --> 00:09:40.500
I want you to kill him.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:48.458
Not physically, of course.
Kill his educational policies.

00:09:48.458 --> 00:09:51.458
His education policies? Like... how?

00:09:51.458 --> 00:09:55.250
Easy. I want you, the E Class,
to dominate the top spots

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.792
in the next end-of-term exams.

00:09:57.792 --> 00:09:59.958
I'll be in first, of course,

00:09:59.958 --> 00:10:03.500
but excellent grades mean nothing
coming from an excellent student.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:07.333
For detritus like you
to show up the A Class, though...

00:10:07.333 --> 00:10:10.125
...<i>that's </i>how we ruin his stance on education.

00:10:10.125 --> 00:10:15.083
Asano, I've heard about the
chilly relationship between you two.

00:10:15.083 --> 00:10:18.833
Are you saying... you want us
to deny your father's methods

00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:20.542
and turn away from him?

00:10:20.542 --> 00:10:22.500
Don't misunderstand.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.708
"Be strong enough
to kick even your father down."

00:10:25.708 --> 00:10:30.042
Or so I've been taught...
and now it's time to put it into practice.

00:10:30.042 --> 00:10:33.833
I don't know about anyone else,
but that's our relationship.

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:38.083
But that's not the case
for the other, lesser students.

00:10:38.083 --> 00:10:42.125
Right now, A Class is hell.

00:10:45.583 --> 00:10:48.125
That's all for today.

00:10:50.042 --> 00:10:53.250
Remember to review.

00:10:56.833 --> 00:11:00.958
--Kill the E Class, kill the E Class, kill the E Class...
--With their hatred for the E Class their only support,

00:11:00.958 --> 00:11:03.583
he's making them study beyond their limits!

00:11:03.583 --> 00:11:05.583
If they win like that...

00:11:05.583 --> 00:11:09.375
...it'll be the only method
they'll trust from now on.

00:11:09.375 --> 00:11:11.375
You can only gain so much strength

00:11:11.375 --> 00:11:15.000
in hating, scorning, misleading your foes.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.333
Even opponents like you
will still give them trouble.

00:11:18.333 --> 00:11:21.625
They'll still be my flunkies in high school.

00:11:21.625 --> 00:11:23.875
But if my flunkies' strength is lopsided,

00:11:23.875 --> 00:11:27.250
I can't rule the ruler.

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:31.708
Sometimes defeat can... open some eyes.

00:11:31.708 --> 00:11:37.958
So please: Show my friends
and my father a proper defeat.

00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:43.333
He's not hiding his arrogant nature

00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:45.958
because he's speaking from his heart.

00:11:45.958 --> 00:11:50.542
This big ball of pride
named Asano is bowing to us.

00:11:50.542 --> 00:11:55.167
He's really, truly worried
about someone who's not him.

00:11:55.167 --> 00:11:58.500
Huh? Is this any time to be
worried about someone else?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:02.167
You're not taking first place--<i>I </i>am.

00:12:03.708 --> 00:12:07.917
I told you: next time the E Class
won't go easy on you.

00:12:07.917 --> 00:12:11.208
I'll be number one, with the rest
of the E Class right under me.

00:12:11.208 --> 00:12:13.792
I'd say tenth place
would look good on you, Asano.

00:12:13.792 --> 00:12:16.625
Ooh, Karma said it! He's taking first place!

00:12:16.625 --> 00:12:20.083
Just don't let it turn out
like it did last time.

00:12:20.083 --> 00:12:23.625
At least try to do better than me, huh?

00:12:24.708 --> 00:12:26.333
Asano,

00:12:26.333 --> 00:12:28.958
we've been trying our best to win all along,

00:12:28.958 --> 00:12:31.042
and we'll do it this time, too.

00:12:31.042 --> 00:12:34.167
That's how it's always been
for us <i>and </i>the A Class.

00:12:34.167 --> 00:12:37.167
We're happy if we win, frustrated if we lose.

00:12:37.167 --> 00:12:39.917
No need for ranks beyond that.

00:12:39.917 --> 00:12:42.542
Isn't that enough?

00:12:42.542 --> 00:12:44.958
We'll do our best so you can all be glad

00:12:44.958 --> 00:12:48.167
you had the chance to take us on.

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:50.958
Don't think too much--

00:12:50.958 --> 00:12:56.625
Just come at us like you want
to kill us. That's what makes it fun.

00:12:56.625 --> 00:13:01.542
How amusing. Then I'll fight
with my gloves off, too.

00:13:02.417 --> 00:13:06.167
Th-These are all for the math exam?!

00:13:06.167 --> 00:13:09.083
Yeah, the principal said to
put together the hardest questions

00:13:09.083 --> 00:13:11.208
out of all this material.

00:13:11.208 --> 00:13:13.458
And this is a <i>junior-high </i>exam?!

00:13:13.458 --> 00:13:16.208
You could get into
a mediocre college with this!

00:13:16.208 --> 00:13:20.083
How high is he trying to
raise the students' level, anyway?

00:13:20.083 --> 00:13:21.417
Hmm?

00:13:21.417 --> 00:13:25.208
Ah, it's unusual to see you here.

00:13:25.208 --> 00:13:28.250
I haven't done anything wrong, Koro Sensei.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:33.750
Yes, I know. You'll go with
orthodox methods till the very end.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:37.708
You wouldn't resort to
cheap tricks this late in the game.

00:13:37.708 --> 00:13:41.583
This will most likely
be our last education battle.

00:13:41.583 --> 00:13:47.417
A thank-you for not rejecting
my presence, for accepting me here.

00:13:48.375 --> 00:13:52.792
Koro Sensei, this is the first school
you've taught at, correct?

00:13:52.792 --> 00:13:54.667
"Educator" "I Am a Teacher!!" "Instructor"
How can you tell?

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:57.375
"Educator" "I Am a Teacher!!" "Instructor"
You're a bit amateurish.

00:13:57.375 --> 00:14:02.083
You won't say a word
about why you became a teacher...

00:14:02.083 --> 00:14:05.375
Perhaps you'll tell me once I win.

00:14:05.375 --> 00:14:08.167
There's not much to tell.

00:14:08.167 --> 00:14:11.250
Broadly speaking, there are only two reasons

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:15.167
a person feels the desire to teach something:

00:14:15.167 --> 00:14:17.833
Either he wants to pass on his successes

00:14:17.833 --> 00:14:20.875
or he wants to pass on his failures.

00:14:20.875 --> 00:14:21.333
"Social Studies" "Structure of the Kamakura Shogunate"

00:14:21.333 --> 00:14:24.625
"Social Studies" "Structure of the Kamakura Shogunate"
Which is it for you, Principal Asano?

00:14:29.792 --> 00:14:31.042
Well, now.

00:14:31.042 --> 00:14:35.042
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Kaede Kayano"

00:14:36.292 --> 00:14:40.042
The second-term finals were one week away.

00:14:40.042 --> 00:14:42.750
We studied our butts off.

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:46.125
We asked Koro Sensei's clones
anything we didn't understand.

00:14:46.125 --> 00:14:49.625
Koro Sensei had his hands so full,

00:14:49.625 --> 00:14:53.417
his clones got really bent out of shape.

00:14:55.958 --> 00:14:59.250
Then the day of battle arrived.

00:15:01.125 --> 00:15:05.083
Kill the E Class,
kill the E Class, kill the E Class...

00:15:05.083 --> 00:15:07.458
Hell of a look in their eyes.

00:15:07.458 --> 00:15:10.292
The A Class is probably
psyching themselves up.

00:15:10.292 --> 00:15:12.042
Can you beat 'em, Karma?

00:15:12.042 --> 00:15:13.833
Who knows?

00:15:13.833 --> 00:15:17.792
If any of them really do plan to kill me,
that <i>might </i>slow me down.

00:15:17.792 --> 00:15:21.542
It was time for the fated
showdown between students

00:15:21.542 --> 00:15:25.583
whose bloodlust had been
cultivated by two monsters.

00:15:25.583 --> 00:15:28.458
We'd slay each other on paper!

00:15:30.958 --> 00:15:31.833
If we get shoddy results here...

00:15:31.833 --> 00:15:33.750
"English"
If we get shoddy results here...

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.000
...we probably won't be able
to hold our heads high

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.417
even if we <i>do </i>pull off the assassination.

00:15:40.542 --> 00:15:42.542
The assassination classroom,

00:15:42.542 --> 00:15:45.250
where we kill and our teacher teaches.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:49.125
And just as he taught us,
we've found our second blades.

00:15:50.667 --> 00:15:53.500
If we can't tell our target as much,

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.833
we can't graduate!

00:15:58.708 --> 00:16:00.208
Time's up!

00:16:03.167 --> 00:16:05.833
It's no good... I couldn't get through 'em.

00:16:05.833 --> 00:16:09.417
Not only are the questions hard,
there are too many of them!

00:16:09.417 --> 00:16:11.458
The listening comprehension test was insane.

00:16:11.458 --> 00:16:15.000
Even Professor Bitch
doesn't have that kind of vocabulary!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.917
Only the first exam,
and we're already this exhausted.

00:16:17.917 --> 00:16:21.583
And English was my best subject!

00:16:21.583 --> 00:16:25.458
Uh-oh. These exams are the real deal.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.167
"Social Studies"

00:16:28.167 --> 00:16:29.000
"Social Studies"
The grade-average line must be far lower than ever before.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:34.708
The grade-average line must be far lower than ever before.

00:16:34.708 --> 00:16:36.625
To get a perfect score...

00:16:36.625 --> 00:16:39.083
If one person in our grade
manages it, it'd be a miracle.

00:16:39.083 --> 00:16:43.750
Which means these exams will
make our standings perfectly clear!

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.042
Take that!

00:16:45.042 --> 00:16:45.917
"Science"

00:16:45.917 --> 00:16:48.250
"Science"
So how's the A Class doing?

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.458
I peeked in on 'em during the break,

00:16:50.458 --> 00:16:52.667
and boy, were they <i>seething</i>.

00:16:57.083 --> 00:16:59.500
Single-mindedly concentrating
like crazy people!

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:02.667
I guess that's how strong
the power of hatred can be.

00:17:02.667 --> 00:17:04.292
"Japanese"
Never mind that--look out!

00:17:04.292 --> 00:17:06.792
We have ourselves to worry about!

00:17:15.917 --> 00:17:17.542
Ritsu?!

00:17:17.542 --> 00:17:22.458
I heard all about it.
We all gotta come in the top fifty.

00:17:22.458 --> 00:17:23.417
Who are <i>you</i>?

00:17:23.417 --> 00:17:25.958
Oh, it's the fake Ritsu.

00:17:25.958 --> 00:17:26.125
The real Ritsu broke it down like this:

00:17:26.125 --> 00:17:29.083
"Fake Ritsu" "Last Midterm Rank: 88th out of 186"
The real Ritsu broke it down like this:

00:17:29.333 --> 00:17:29.417
Reaching that goal hinges on lower-scorers like me working hard.

00:17:29.417 --> 00:17:31.875
"Justice Kimura: 91st out of 186" "Hiroto Maehara: 101st out of 186"
Reaching that goal hinges on lower-scorers like me working hard.

00:17:31.875 --> 00:17:35.917
"Hinata Okano: 108th out of 186" "Sosuke Sugaya: 126th out of 186"
Reaching that goal hinges on lower-scorers like me working hard.

00:17:38.375 --> 00:17:39.750
We're just gonna have to do it!

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.292
Begin!

00:17:41.292 --> 00:17:44.667
With the unusual number
and difficulty of these questions,

00:17:44.667 --> 00:17:48.792
you have to decide how to
pace yourself the second you see them.

00:17:48.792 --> 00:17:50.750
If you hesitate about where to strike...

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.000
"Mathematics"
If you hesitate about where to strike...

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.708
"Mathematics"
...you'll be cornered before you know it.

00:17:55.667 --> 00:17:59.333
Seems the one we were
most worried about is doing all right.

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:04.583
Is Terasaka for real?

00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:06.833
It's a die probability problem.

00:18:06.833 --> 00:18:08.708
He's crushing it by using brute force

00:18:08.708 --> 00:18:11.042
to go through all the
potential answers one by one.

00:18:11.042 --> 00:18:14.000
Aren't you supposed to
use a combination equation?

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:18.167
Nah, that's a good strategy
for a simple, honest lunkhead like him.

00:18:18.167 --> 00:18:21.208
If you hesitate while
fishing around for efficiency,

00:18:21.208 --> 00:18:23.708
sometimes it's faster to score the first strike

00:18:23.708 --> 00:18:27.000
and crush them all
the second you see the question.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:27.958
"Tentacle" "Terasaka's Math Notes"

00:18:27.958 --> 00:18:30.417
"Tentacle" "Terasaka's Math Notes"
When you have this and this here,

00:18:30.417 --> 00:18:33.875
"Tentacle" "Terasaka's Math Notes"
don't hesitate--use the strategy I've just taught you.

00:18:33.875 --> 00:18:36.000
Simplicity is your forte.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:39.375
A feat of strength like this
suits you best! Squish squish!

00:18:39.375 --> 00:18:41.167
That damn octopus!

00:18:41.167 --> 00:18:43.792
Just 'cause I'm an idiot
don't mean he can treat me like one!

00:18:43.792 --> 00:18:46.417
We could stand to learn from his dorkiness.

00:18:46.417 --> 00:18:47.333
Yeah.

00:18:47.333 --> 00:18:50.167
We <i>are </i>the End Class, after all!

00:18:50.167 --> 00:18:53.583
No time for acting cool--
we gotta do it quick and dirty!

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.000
Zero in on your target's weakness.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.833
You can weaken it in one round
if you hit it enough!

00:18:59.833 --> 00:19:02.375
Even if you don't get the right answer...

00:19:02.375 --> 00:19:04.958
...if your approach is correct...

00:19:04.958 --> 00:19:07.333
...you can at least pick up...

00:19:07.333 --> 00:19:09.042
...partial credit!

00:19:10.958 --> 00:19:13.542
All right! That probably did the trick!

00:19:13.542 --> 00:19:16.833
No time to review! Move on! Next!

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:26.833
Hey, now--

00:19:26.833 --> 00:19:27.083
"Find the general formula for a[n] as defined"
Hey, now--

00:19:27.083 --> 00:19:28.458
"Find the general formula for a[n] as defined"
recurrence relations, right before the end?!

00:19:28.458 --> 00:19:30.542
"in the following recurrence-relation sequence {a[n]}."
recurrence relations, right before the end?!

00:19:30.542 --> 00:19:33.042
I thought it only existed in rumors.

00:19:33.042 --> 00:19:35.917
For it to show up on a junior-high exam...!

00:19:38.167 --> 00:19:40.083
Yikes! Mayday, mayday!

00:19:40.083 --> 00:19:42.667
M-My ammo's not ready!

00:19:52.375 --> 00:19:54.458
It's not working!

00:19:57.167 --> 00:19:58.583
Karma!

00:20:09.917 --> 00:20:12.125
You have to take it to a particular solution.

00:20:12.125 --> 00:20:14.958
I taught you how last week.

00:20:14.958 --> 00:20:17.083
In addition to their classes,

00:20:17.083 --> 00:20:20.917
this time I had the students
teach each other their best subjects.

00:20:20.917 --> 00:20:25.250
By teaching someone else,
you deepen your own understanding

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:26.167
and, more than anything, strengthen teamwork.

00:20:26.167 --> 00:20:28.500
"Russo-Japanese Convention" "Japanese History"
and, more than anything, strengthen teamwork.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.167
It had an immediate effect
on Karma in particular.

00:20:31.167 --> 00:20:34.708
It patched over his gaps
and gave him a more perfect finish.

00:20:34.708 --> 00:20:38.500
But that Asano boy's an overachiever, too.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:39.958
Yes.

00:20:39.958 --> 00:20:43.917
No longer the one responsible
for improving his class,

00:20:43.917 --> 00:20:48.542
he put those efforts into
polishing his own blade instead.

00:20:48.542 --> 00:20:51.542
That's another way to respond to strength.

00:20:51.542 --> 00:20:55.875
Even I don't know which is better.

00:21:05.667 --> 00:21:08.083
Everyone just calm down and solve it.

00:21:08.083 --> 00:21:10.667
You should at least get partial credit.

00:21:10.667 --> 00:21:14.792
I'll get all your full-marks answers.

00:21:23.875 --> 00:21:25.708
Now, then...

00:21:25.708 --> 00:21:28.667
How shall I finish him off?

00:21:42.542 --> 00:21:48.042
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:48.042 --> 00:21:53.417
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:53.417 --> 00:21:59.083
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:59.083 --> 00:22:04.250
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:15.625
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.625 --> 00:22:21.208
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:21.208 --> 00:22:25.625
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.625 --> 00:22:32.458
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.458 --> 00:22:37.958
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:37.958 --> 00:22:43.458
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.458 --> 00:23:02.144
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
